      en: "The Knesset, Israel's unicameral national legislature, is located in Jerusalem's Givat Ram neighborhood. Completed in 1966, the building is an example of modernist brutalist architecture, clad in Jerusalem stone. It houses 120 members of parliament who debate and pass laws, approve the budget, and oversee the government. The plenary hall features a giant bronze chandelier and a raised podium. The Knesset complex also includes the Knesset Menorah, a 4-meter-high bronze sculpture depicting Jewish historical figures and events. Visits are available for the public, offering insight into Israeli democracy.",
