      en: "Damascus Gate is one of the main entrances to the Old City of Jerusalem, located on the northern wall. It was built in the 16th century under Sultan Suleiman the Magnificent. The gate features elaborate crenellations and a pointed arch. It leads to the Muslim and Christian Quarters. The plaza in front is a bustling hub with markets, food stalls, and bus stops. Its name derives from the road leading to Damascus. The gate is part of the Ottoman city walls, constructed between 1538 and 1541.",
