      en: "The Eretz Israel Museum is a sprawling cultural institution in Tel Aviv, established in 1958. Its campus features themed pavilions covering archaeology, ethnography, and Judaica, set in a large park with reconstructed ancient industries. The site includes the excavated Philistine port city of Tell Qasile, which yielded artifacts from the 12th century BCE. The museum holds over 100,000 items, including a renowned glass collection and a coin cabinet with thousands of specimens. Outdoor exhibits showcase an olive press, a pottery kiln, and a 19th-century windmill. With around 200,000 annual visitors, the museum also runs extensive school programs and temporary exhibitions on contemporary Israeli culture.",
