      en: "The Chords Bridge in Jerusalem, designed by Santiago Calatrava, opened in 2008. This 360-meter-long cable-stayed bridge features a single 118-meter pylon from which cables fan out like harp strings, symbolizing King David's harp. It carries the Jerusalem Light Rail as well as pedestrians and cyclists, linking the city center with the Kiryat HaYovel neighborhood. The bridge is made of steel and concrete, with a deck width of 14.8 meters. Its construction cost approximately €130 million. The Chords Bridge has become an iconic modern addition to Jerusalem's skyline and a popular tourist attraction.",
