      en: "The Rockefeller Museum in East Jerusalem opened in 1938, funded by John D. Rockefeller Jr. Designed by British architect Austen St. Barbe Harrison, the building blends Western and Eastern architectural styles, including Islamic, Byzantine, and Gothic elements. It houses an extensive archaeological collection spanning prehistory to the Ottoman Empire, excavated from sites across Palestine. Notable artifacts include the Lachish Letters, written in ancient Hebrew on pottery, and a large collection of coins. The museum served as the main repository for the Israeli Antiquities Authority. Its central courtyard features a stone fountain. The museum remains a key institution for Near Eastern archaeology.",
