      en: "The Lions Fountain in Jerusalem is located on Teddy Kollek Square, near the City Hall. Created in 1993 by Israeli sculptor Ygael Tumarkin, the fountain features a large circular basin with a central bronze lion statue spouting water, surrounded by smaller lion figures. The fountain is a popular meeting point and a symbol of Jerusalem. It was funded by donations and is part of the larger square, which often hosts public events and celebrations. The fountain is illuminated at night, adding to the square's vibrant atmosphere.",
