      en: "The Suzanne Dellal Centre for Dance and Theatre in Tel Aviv, opened in 1989, is a premier venue for contemporary dance and performing arts. Located in the historic Neve Tzedek neighborhood, it is named after philanthropist Suzanne Dellal. The center houses multiple performance spaces, including the Yerushalmi Theatre (400 seats) and a studio theatre. It is the home of the Batsheva Dance Company, renowned worldwide for its innovative repertoire. The complex includes a courtyard café and hosts festivals like the International Exposure. The center is a cultural hub, fostering dance and theatre in Israel.",
